From: Collins Ikechukwu <collinschristroa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:19:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] scf: random daily session salt held only in Redis

SCF_RANDOM_DAILY_SALT replaces the date-derived session salt with a random
salt per UTC day. It is stored in Redis with a 48-hour TTL (process memory
when Redis is not configured) and never written to the database. Once it
expires, stored session ids cannot be linked back to an IP and user agent,
even by someone holding APP_SECRET.

Applied in resolveIdentifiedSession, so /api/send and error collection agree.
